of natural leadership skills.

00:02:06.051 --> 00:02:09.497
For me, the reason I aspired
to be a great leader is

00:02:09.497 --> 00:02:12.052
I truly focused on one
variable, and I want everybody

00:02:12.052 --> 00:02:14.977
to hear this, and it's
a very sneaky pillar

00:02:14.977 --> 00:02:17.646
of my life success, which
is, when I think about you,

00:02:17.646 --> 00:02:22.116
India, or you DRock, or
anybody that I jam with

00:02:22.116 --> 00:02:25.134
in my world, start-ups, companies,

00:02:25.134 --> 00:02:27.514
when I go to Oklahoma City, the client,

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:31.230
I'm trying to provide 51% of a value.

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.412
I really believe that,
and not because I'm this

00:02:33.412 --> 00:02:35.653
great human being, because
I think it's leverage.

00:02:35.653 --> 00:02:38.636
I think that if DRock feels
that I'm slightly providing

00:02:38.636 --> 00:02:41.028
more value to him than
he's providing to me,

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:44.627
financially, upside in
the future, mentorship,

00:02:44.627 --> 00:02:46.647
whatever it may be, that that's

00:02:46.647 --> 00:02:48.550
